lates, project scaffolds, document templates, agent templates like OpenClaw SOUL.md configs). Tagged with `kind='template'` in the schema; lighter-weight validation (no runner exec â€” they're not directly runnable).\n- Promoted the **dual-axis** framing in Â§7 to be explicit: *what it does* Ã— *how complex a task it handles*. Both axes apply uniformly across all four artifact kinds.\n- Added Â§15 â€” **Helping Hand**, a meta-skill that runs in any Cowork/Claude Code session and recommends from the KB. Default mode: approve-then-load. Skill + MCP server packaged together as `helping-hand.plugin`.\n- Added Â§16 â€” **GitHub collaborator distribution**. Single private repo. Publisher stage commits scrubbed `kb-snapshot.sqlite` (no transcripts), full markdown library, and the latest `helping-hand.plugin` after each nightly cycle. Daily `YYYYMMDD` tags.\n\n**Change log v2 â†’ v3**\n- All 10 Â§17 open questions resolved; decisions are committed and visible in Â§17 (renamed \"Decisions logged\").\n- Added Â§9.4 â€” **08:30 morning briefing** as a Cowork scheduled session that consolidates the three exec summaries, surfaces budget, and renders PAT expiry reminders.\n- Added **budget tracking** end-to-end: `costs` table in Â§6 schema, one-line budget block in every exec summary, full breakdown + 7-day trend + cap-projection warnings in the morning briefing. Dedicated Aurora-scoped Anthropic + Gemini keys with monthly caps ($50 / $10 to start).\n- Added **PAT expiry surfacing** in the morning briefing (7/3/1 days); publisher hard-fails-loud on 401 with a `PAT_EXPIRED.txt` in the workspace folder.\n- Set Aurora root to **`C:\\dev\\aurora\\`** (top-level, separate from this planning folder).\n- Docker locked as the runner sandbox; Windows Task Scheduler locked as primary scheduler; Gemini locked as Critic B primary with a configurable local-LLM fallback.\n\n**Change log v3 â†’ v4 (post-launch reconciliation, 2026-05-18)**\n- Added Â§18 (post-deployment status) â€” what's actually working vs. partial vs. gapped, including the overnight-outage incident and the hardening pass that followed.\n- Added Â§19 (Ghost World Labs / OpenClaw integration scope) â€” non-executing sketch of how Helping Hand drops into GWL's GBrain-resolved OpenClaw agent stack. To be executed in a Cowork session opened inside `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home`, not from this curator project.\n- Added Â§20 (next-steps punch list) â€” 14 items prioritized by impact Ã— effort across this-week / 1-2-weeks / later. Includes sunburst, neural_plasticity populate, template-detection heuristic, dedicated keys, GWL integration, threshold calibration, P9 trigger.\n- Documented hardening pass that wasn't in the v3 plan: publisher logging, launcher logging, missed-run watchdog, hybrid YAML parser, WakeToRun + StartWhenAvailable, Active Hours + 03:00 reboot pin, cross-runtime HH install, collaborator distribution.\n- Factual corrections: Hermes star count (~95K, not 140K), GBrain storage (Postgres+pgvector with MCP *interface*, not \"MCP-based memory\"), OpenClaw governance (steering committee, not Steinberger).\n- Added prompt-injection quarantine stage between scout and screener.\n- Made critic independence structural, not aspirational â€” different input streams + at least one cross-vendor critic.\n- GitHub dedupe rewritten around canonical normalization + aliases table.\n- Reproducibility: per-run snapshots of seed maps, prompt templates, model IDs.\n- Honest framing on the hyperbolic map (v1 = sunburst; learned-hyperbolic only at â‰¥500 artifacts).\n- Sweep queueing with a global lock file.\n- Interestingness decay added.\n- Clone-don't-import isolation for license/legal hygiene.\n- Seed maps expanded with verified additions (Letta v1, Mem0, MemoryAgentBench, official MCP Registry, Smithery, MCPfinder, awesome-claude-skills, claude-plugins.dev, Anthropic memory tool docs, Anthropic \"dreaming\" preview, Simon Willison's annotated system prompts).\n- Neural-plasticity schema expanded with 